# Find accessibility problems

SEED.html can check the chapter you are working on for problems that make a book hard to use with a screen reader or other assistive technology, such as a picture with no description or headings that skip a level.

1. Click the check button above the preview, beside [Reader]{.ui}. The [Accessibility]{.ui} panel opens above the preview and checks the chapter, with one line for each problem.
2. Read a problem. Click [learn more]{.ui} for a full explanation and how to fix it.
3. In the preview, the part of the page with the problem has a red outline. Click it to find the same place in the editor.
4. Fix the text. While the panel is open, the check runs again as you type.

The button shows how many problems the last check found. Each chapter is checked on its own: open each chapter in turn, with the panel open, before you package the book.
